{"type":"message","id":"cbd27791","parentId":"15ca48bc","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:16:04.080Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-03-08 23:13 GMT+1] You are an expert AI systems architect.\n\n**Context:**\n- OpenClaw neuro-memory + evolution integration\n- Need to measure if the integration is actually helping\n- Evolution runs weekly, generates proposals, tests them, applies successful ones\n\n**Question:** How do we measure success of neuro-memory → evolution integration?\n\nWhat metrics to track:\n- Proposal quality (acceptance rate, survival time)\n- Failure reduction (same error recurring?)\n- Performance impact (hot path latency)\n- Learning velocity (how fast patterns emerge)\n\nGive me:\n- 5-7 specific metrics with formulas\n- How to collect each metric\n- What \"good\" looks like (baseline vs improved)\n- Dashboard/alerting recommendations\n- A/B test design (evolution with vs without neuro-memory)\n\nBe specific and opinionated."}],"timestamp":1773008164079}}
{"type":"message","id":"dd356c06","parentId":"cbd27791","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:17:26.275Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a comprehensive metrics framework for measuring the success of a neuro-memory integration with an evolution system. This is a technical architecture question about AI systems.\n\nLet me structure this:\n\n1. 5-7 specific metrics with formulas\n2. How to collect each\n3. Baseline vs improved benchmarks\n4. Dashboard/alerting recommendations\n5. A/B test design\n\nI need to be specific and opinionated. Let me think about what metrics would actually matter:\n\n1. **Proposal Acceptance Rate** - Are memory-informed proposals better?\n2. **Error Recurrence Rate** - Are we actually learning from failures?\n3. **Time to Pattern Recognition** - How fast do we identify patterns?\n4. **Proposal Survival Time** - How long do changes stick?\n5. **Regression Rate** - Do \"improvements\" cause new issues?\n6. **Hot Path Latency Delta** - Performance impact\n7. **Memory Utilization Score** - Is the memory actually being used?\n\nLet me be very specific with formulas and collection methods.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"# Neuro-Memory → Evolution Integration: Success Metrics Framework\n\n## 1. Core Metrics (5-7)\n\n### 1.1 Proposal Acceptance Rate (PAR)\n**What it measures:** Quality of evolution proposals informed by neuro-memory vs baseline\n\n```\nPAR = (Proposals_Accepted / Total_Proposals_Generated) × 100\n\nPAR_memory = PAR for memory-informed proposals\nPAR_baseline = PAR for proposals without memory context\n\nDelta_PAR = PAR_memory - PAR_baseline\n```\n\n**Collection:**\n- Tag each proposal with `memory_informed: true/false`\n- Track in evolution history: `proposalId`, `source`, `outcome`\n- Calculate weekly\n\n**Good looks like:**\n| State | PAR |\n|-------|-----|\n| Baseline (no memory) | 30-40% |\n| With memory | 50-65% |\n| Delta | +15-25% |\n\n**Alert if:** `Delta_PAR < +10%` for 3 consecutive weeks\n\n---\n\n### 1.2 Error Recurrence Rate (ERR)\n**What it measures:** Whether memory actually prevents repeat failures\n\n```\nERR = (Repeated_Errors / Total_Errors) × 100\n\nRepeated_Error = error signature matching a pattern in neuro-memory\n               that was marked \"resolved\" >7 days ago\n```\n\n**Collection:**\n- Hash error signatures (stack trace + context)\n- Query neuro-memory for matching patterns\n- Flag if pattern exists with `status: resolved`\n- Track daily, aggregate weekly\n\n**Good looks like:**\n| State | ERR |\n|-------|-----|\n| Baseline | 25-35% |\n| With memory | 8-15% |\n| Improvement | 50-70% reduction |\n\n**Alert if:** `ERR > 20%` for any week\n\n---\n\n### 1.3 Time-to-Pattern (T2P)\n**What it measures:** Learning velocity - how fast patterns emerge and get codified\n\n```\nT2P = median(time_from_first_error_to_pattern_codified)\n\nT2P_memory = T2P when memory integration active\nT2P_baseline = T2P from historical data\n```\n\n**Collection:**\n- Log `first_seen` timestamp for each error pattern\n- Log `codified_at` when pattern becomes actionable proposal\n- Calculate median across all patterns in time window\n\n**Good looks like:**\n| State | T2P |\n|-------|-----|\n| Baseline | 14-21 days |\n| With memory | 3-7 days |\n| Improvement | 3-5x faster |\n\n**Alert if:** `T2P > 10 days` for 2 consecutive weeks\n\n---\n\n### 1.4 Proposal Survival Half-Life (PSH)\n**What it measures:** How long proposals stick before being reverted/modified\n\n```\nPSH = time at which 50% of proposals are still active\n\nFor each proposal:\n  - birth: applied_at\n  - death: reverted_at OR significant_modification_at\n  - age_at_week_N = death - birth (or now - birth if alive)\n```\n\n**Collection:**\n- Tag proposals with version chain\n- Track reversions and major modifications\n- Calculate survival curve weekly\n\n**Good looks like:**\n| State | PSH |\n|-------|-----|\n| Baseline | 30-45 days |\n| With memory | 60-90 days |\n| Improvement | 2x longer |\n\n**Alert if:** `PSH < 21 days` for memory-informed proposals\n\n---\n\n### 1.5 Regression Rate (RR)\n**What it measures:** Whether proposals introduce new failures\n\n```\nRR = (Proposals_That_Caused_Regressions / Total_Proposals_Applied) × 100\n\nRegression = new error pattern appearing within 7 days of proposal application\n             in code paths the proposal touched\n```\n\n**Collection:**\n- Map proposals to affected files/modules\n- Monitor error logs for 7 days post-application\n- Correlate new errors with changed code paths\n\n**Good looks like:**\n| State | RR |\n|-------|-----|\n| Baseline | 15-25% |\n| With memory | 5-10% |\n| Improvement | 50%+ reduction |\n\n**Alert if:** `RR > 12%` for memory-informed proposals\n\n---\n\n### 1.6 Hot Path Latency Delta (HPLD)\n**What it measures:** Performance impact of evolution changes\n\n```\nHPLD = p95_latency_after_proposal - p95_latency_before_proposal\n\nMeasured for critical hot paths:\n  - Memory retrieval (p95 < 50ms baseline)\n  - Evolution proposal generation (p95 < 5s baseline)\n  - Pattern matching queries (p95 < 20ms baseline)\n\nHPLD_memory_avg = mean(HPLD) for memory-informed proposals\n```\n\n**Collection:**\n- Instrument hot paths with timing\n- Snapshot latency before/after each proposal\n- Exclude proposals that don't touch hot paths\n\n**Good looks like:**\n| State | HPLD (avg) |\n|-------|------------|\n| Baseline | ±2-5ms noise |\n| With memory | 0 to +3ms |\n| Maximum acceptable | +10ms |\n\n**Alert if:** `HPLD > +10ms` for any hot path\n\n---\n\n### 1.7 Memory Utilization Score (MUS)\n**What it measures:** Is the memory actually being used in decisions?\n\n```\nMUS = (Proposals_Using_Memory_Patterns / Total_Proposals) × 100\n\nMemory_Usage = proposal cites ≥1 neuro-memory pattern ID\n```\n\n**Collection:**\n- Require memory query log for each proposal\n- Tag proposals with `memory_patterns_used: [ids]`\n- Track pattern hit rate\n\n**Good looks like:**\n| State | MUS |\n|-------|-----|\n| Week 1-2 | 20-30% (learning) |\n| Week 3-4 | 50-60% (ramping) |\n| Steady state | 70-85% |\n| Over-reliance | >95% (may indicate no novelty) |\n\n**Alert if:** `MUS < 40%` after 4 weeks OR `MUS > 95%` for 2 weeks\n\n---\n\n## 2. Dashboard Layout\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Neuro-Memory → Evolution Dashboard                              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐          │\n│  │ PAR          │  │ ERR          │  │ T2P          │          │\n│  │ 58% (+18) ✅ │  │ 12% (-18) ✅ │  │ 5d (-12d) ✅ │          │\n│  │ ▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█    │  │ █▇▆▅▄▃▂▁    │  │ █▇▆▅▄▃▂▁    │          │\n│  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘          │\n│                                                                  │\n│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐          │\n│  │ PSH          │  │ RR           │  │ MUS          │          │\n│  │ 72d (+30) ✅ │  │ 8% (-10) ✅  │  │ 73% 🟢       │          │\n│  │ ▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█    │  │ █▇▆▅▄▃▂▁    │  │ ▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█    │          │\n│  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘          │\n│                                                                  │\n│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ HPLD (Hot Path Latency Delta)                              │  │\n│  │ Memory Retrieval: +2ms  │  Proposal Gen: -1ms  │  Match: +4ms│  │\n│  │ 🟢🟢🟢🟢🟢🟢🟢🟢🟡🟢  (all within SLA)                      │  │\n│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n│                                                                  │\n│  [Week-over-Week Trend]  [Memory vs Baseline Comparison]         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Alert Configuration:**\n```yaml\nalerts:\n  - name: low_proposal_quality\n    condition: Delta_PAR < 10% for 3 weeks\n    severity: warning\n    channel: #evolution-alerts\n    \n  - name: error_recurrence_high\n    condition: ERR > 20%\n    severity: critical\n    channel: #evolution-alerts\n    \n  - name: slow_learning\n    condition: T2P > 10 days for 2 weeks\n    severity: warning\n    channel: #evolution-alerts\n    \n  - name: high_regression\n    condition: RR > 12% for memory-informed\n    severity: critical\n    channel: #evolution-alerts\n    \n  - name: performance_degradation\n    condition: HPLD > 10ms for any hot path\n    severity: critical\n    channel: #evolution-alerts\n    \n  - name: memory_underutilized\n    condition: MUS < 40% after week 4\n    severity: warning\n    channel: #evolution-alerts\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. A/B Test Design\n\n### Experimental Setup\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                EVOLUTION A/B TEST                        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                          │\n│   Population: All evolution proposals                    │\n│                                                          │\n│   ┌─────────────┐        ┌─────────────┐               │\n│   │   Group A   │        │   Group B   │               │\n│   │  (Control)  │        │ (Treatment) │               │\n│   │             │        │             │               │\n│   │  NO memory  │        │  WITH mem   │               │\n│   │  context    │        │  context    │               │\n│   │             │        │             │               │\n│   │   50% of    │        │   50% of    │               │\n│   │  proposals  │        │  proposals  │               │\n│   └─────────────┘        └─────────────┘               │\n│                                                          │\n│   Duration: 8 weeks minimum                              │\n│   Sample: ~200 proposals per group                       │\n│                                                          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Assignment Strategy\n\n```typescript\n// Deterministic assignment based on proposal ID hash\nfunction assignGroup(proposalId: string): 'A' | 'B' {\n  const hash = sha256(proposalId + SALT);\n  const bucket = parseInt(hash.slice(0, 8), 16) % 100;\n  return bucket < 50 ? 'A' : 'B';\n}\n\n// Ensure balanced assignment per week\nfunction validateBalance(weekProposals: Proposal[]): boolean {\n  const groupA = weekProposals.filter(p => p.group === 'A').length;\n  const groupB = weekProposals.length - groupA;\n  return Math.abs(groupA - groupB) / weekProposals.length < 0.1; // <10% imbalance\n}\n```\n\n### Metrics Comparison\n\n| Metric | Hypothesis | Success Criteria |\n|--------|------------|------------------|\n| PAR | B > A | p < 0.05, effect size > 0.3 |\n| ERR | B < A | p < 0.01, effect size > 0.5 |\n| T2P | B < A | p < 0.05, effect size > 0.4 |\n| PSH | B > A | p < 0.05, effect size > 0.3 |\n| RR | B < A | p < 0.05, effect size > 0.3 |\n| HPLD | B ≈ A | no significant degradation |\n\n### Statistical Analysis\n\n```python\n# Primary analysis: Two-sample tests\nfrom scipy import stats\n\ndef analyze_ab_test(group_a, group_b, metric_name):\n    # For rates/proportions: Chi-square or Fisher exact\n    if metric_name in ['PAR', 'ERR', 'RR']:\n        contingency = [[a_success, a_total - a_success],\n                       [b_success, b_total - b_success]]\n        chi2, p_value = stats.chi2_contingency(contingency)[:2]\n    \n    # For continuous: Mann-Whitney U (robust to non-normal)\n    else:\n        stat, p_value = stats.mannwhitneyu(group_a, group_b)\n    \n    # Effect size (Cohen's d)\n    pooled_std = np.sqrt((np.std(group_a)**2 + np.std(group_b)**2) / 2)\n    cohens_d = (np.mean(group_b) - np.mean(group_a)) / pooled_std\n    \n    return {\n        'p_value': p_value,\n        'effect_size': cohens_d,\n        'significant': p_value < 0.05 and abs(cohens_d) > 0.3\n    }\n```\n\n### Rollout Criteria\n\n**Phase 1 (Weeks 1-4):** 50/50 split, monitor for issues\n- Check HPLD daily for degradation\n- Abort if RR spikes >25% in either group\n\n**Phase 2 (Weeks 5-8):** Continue 50/50, collect statistical power\n- Minimum 100 proposals per group\n- Calculate confidence intervals\n\n**Phase 3 (Decision Point):**\n```\nIF 3+ metrics show significant improvement (p < 0.05, d > 0.3)\n   AND no metric shows significant degradation\n   AND HPLD within SLA\nTHEN\n   Roll memory integration to 100%\n   Continue monitoring for 4 weeks\nELSE\n   Investigate, tune, or abort\n```\n\n**Guardrails:**\n- Automatic rollback if RR > 30% in treatment group\n- Manual review required if ERR doesn't improve by week 6\n- Weekly check-in on statistical power (n > 100 per group by week 4)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Checklist\n\n### Week 0 (Setup)\n- [ ] Add `memory_informed` tag to proposal schema\n- [ ] Instrument hot paths with latency tracking\n- [ ] Set up error signature hashing\n- [ ] Configure A/B assignment logic\n- [ ] Deploy dashboard\n\n### Week 1-2 (Baseline)\n- [ ] Run with Group A only (no memory) to establish baseline\n- [ ] Validate metrics collection\n- [ ] Tune alert thresholds based on noise\n\n### Week 3-10 (A/B Test)\n- [ ] Enable 50/50 split\n- [ ] Monitor daily for anomalies\n- [ ] Weekly metric reviews\n- [ ] Statistical analysis at weeks 4, 6, 8\n\n### Week 11+ (Rollout)\n- [ ] Decision on full rollout\n- [ ] Gradual ramp if approved (75% → 100%)\n- [ ] Continued monitoring\n\n---\n\n## 5. Opinionated Takes\n\n**Most critical metric:** ERR (Error Recurrence Rate)\n- This is the *whole point* of memory - not making the same mistakes\n- If this doesn't improve, the integration is failing its primary purpose\n\n**Hardest to get right:** T2P (Time-to-Pattern)\n- Requires careful tracking of \"first seen\" vs \"codified\"\n- Easy to game by codifying too early\n- Needs human review for quality\n\n**Most likely to fail:** MUS (Memory Utilization Score)\n- Integration bugs often cause memory to not be queried\n- Low MUS is a leading indicator of other metric failures\n- Monitor this first and most frequently\n\n**My recommendation:** Start with 4-week baseline (no memory at all), then 8-week A/B test. Don't shortcut the baseline - you need clean comparison data.\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Metric | Formula | Target Improvement | Collection Freq | Alert Threshold |\n|--------|---------|-------------------|-----------------|-----------------|\n| PAR | accepted/generated | +15-25% | Weekly | < +10% for 3wk |\n| ERR | repeated/total | -50-70% | Daily | > 20% any week |\n| T2P | median(codified - first) | 3-5x faster | Daily | > 10d for 2wk |\n| PSH | 50% survival time | 2x longer | Weekly | < 21d |\n| RR | regressions/applied | -50% | Weekly | > 12% |\n| HPLD | p95_after - p95_before | < +10ms | Continuous | > +10ms |\n| MUS | with_memory/total | 70-85% | Weekly | < 40% or > 95% |\n\nThis framework is opinionated but measurable. Adjust thresholds based on your actual baselines, but the structure should hold."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zhipu","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":2851,"output":4021,"cacheRead":11264,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18136,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773008164080}}
